# F-02 planner-owned acceptance baseline — REVISION 3 (read-only)
#
# Prepared 2026-10-04 by the planner/test-owner session, after the independent
# implementation review (docs/reviews/F-02.md, CHANGES_REQUIRED) and the
# revision-2 preparation re-review (docs/reviews/F-02-preparation-revision-2.md,
# Q1-Q4). F-01 remains accepted; its historical result is unchanged.
#
# REVISION HISTORY
#   rev 1  2026-10-03  20 entries. Superseded.
#   rev 2  2026-10-03  24 entries; verified 24/24 at the implementation review.
#                   ARCHIVED byte-for-byte at docs/handoffs/F-02-tests-rev2.sha256.
#                   The archive's own SHA-256 is
#                   fbfc5c159a8aa3b93a5a6cd7648081b5c885ac1962225279e4977b9e75299c89,
#                   exactly the value recorded for the active manifest in
#                   docs/reviews/F-02-inspected.sha256 — so the archive is provably
#                   the manifest the independent reviewer inspected.
#                   Do not regenerate the archive. Running sha256sum -c on it now
#                   yields 15 OK / 9 FAILED: the nine failures are precisely the
#                   planner-owned artifacts this revision legitimately corrects.
#   rev 3 follow-up (same day, still unapproved): a review follow-up closed two
#                   test-strength gaps before the independent preparation re-review:
#                   the R3 integration candidates are now asserted as EXACT stored
#                   sets with explicit exclusions (fabricated/unauthorised options
#                   fail), and the tablet R3 test now uses a selection-consistent
#                   success fixture plus no-pre-selection, no-extra-option and
#                   credentials-retained assertions. The integration test, tablet
#                   auth suite and the feature spec/plan were refreshed again; the
#                   mutation evidence is in docs/handoffs/F-02-prepared.md.
#   rev 3  2026-10-04  24 entries, same paths, 9 refreshes. Changes only:
#                   - Corrected Q1 (explicit credential injection into every auth
#                     test factory plus a fail-closed-when-omitted case), Q3 (root
#                     /challans/:id path with a known-record control read) and Q4
#                     (distinct usernames, valid control, required role_mismatch)
#                     in apps/api/tests/integration/f02-auth.test.ts.
#                   - Corrected Q2 (form-based authenticated precondition, token
#                     required on session lookup, storage isolation) in both
#                     foundation component suites.
#                   - Added R1 (client role boundary, fresh and restored), R2
#                     (stale restoration ordering around login and logout) and R3
#                     (tablet explicit context selection) to both client auth
#                     suites.
#                   - Added R1 browser refusal journeys (real API sessions, fresh
#                     and restored) to both auth browser specs.
#                   - Reconciled the ambiguous-context contract, zero-shift
#                     refusal, malformed-ID handling, client role/ordering rules
#                     and storage seam in specs/003-demo-auth/spec.md and
#                     refreshed the plan for the correction batch.
#
# Earlier baselines remain unchanged and must continue to verify:
#   docs/handoffs/S-01-tests.sha256            11 entries
#   docs/handoffs/F-01-tests.sha256            14 entries
#   docs/handoffs/F-01-corrections-tests.sha256 10 entries
# docs/reviews/F-01-accepted.sha256 still reports 28/33, with exactly the five
